Stereo 3D in the edition's one format (ORDER 39): both eyes as complete pictures, side by side, left eye first, declared to Stereo KWin; OpenGL draws them into a window the desktop makes two views wide, Vulkan into two image layers the graphics driver packs and declares.

Dolphin's own Depth and Convergence, the per-game Depth Percentage, Convergence and Monoscopic Shadows, and their hotkeys are upstream's, with upstream's defaults; the program's other stereo output modes and its eye swap are not built (the desktop's outputs make every format, the eye swap is the output's).

3D is on by default: a desktop that cannot take the pair shows 2D and says nothing unless the person turned 3D on; a renderer or Vulkan surface that cannot give two views is told; the interface and the on-screen messages are drawn in both eyes; the no-GUI front end shows 2D and says so. The new sentences in pl, pt_BR, fr, de, es, ja, ko, zh_CN and zh_TW.

The Dolphin emulator breaks Mesa's Vulkan drivers older than 26.1.6-1+stereo3d29 (ORDER 774): up to +stereo3d28 a Vulkan X11 window could report half its width (Mesa patch 0047), and the emulator then drew each eye at half the width in about four sessions of ten. apt installs this package only together with the fixed Mesa.
